From c8e92a3263818dc898490558015d9bf9ca7d6937 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oneup03 <oneup03@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:10:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Asynchronous audio tasks; report RSP completions at
 submission

An SDK-style audio manager builds its next task only after the previous
one's completion message, and the game's scheduler starts tasks only at
a retrace. With an audio microcode that takes most of a retrace interval
(an interpreter on a 3DS at the Old 3DS clock: 10 to 17 ms a task) the
manager misses every other retrace, produces two thirds of the samples
the DAC plays, and the music runs slow and breaks up.

ultramodern::set_async_audio_tasks(true) reports an audio task complete
when it is submitted. The task thread runs it from a copy taken then (the
game may reuse its OSTask). The buffers the game hands to
osAiSetNextBuffer are kept until the tasks submitted by then have run and
passed to the host by the task thread; osAiGetLength counts them as
queued meanwhile; and osAiSetNextBuffer holds the game while two tasks
are outstanding, whose command lists and output buffers the game is
about to reuse. Opt-in, for a game that takes every task's output through
osAiSetNextBuffer alone.

The RSP completion of a graphics task is now sent from submit_rsp_task
itself instead of through the task thread, where it would wait behind a
running audio task.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
